Subject: [PATCH] Molten Core: Sulfuron priests die first and are interrupted, one healer follows the Living Bomb

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

Sulfuron Harbinger stands with four Flamewaker Priests (11662). Their Dark
Mending (19775) heals them faster than the raid kills, and the bots spread
their damage over Sulfuron and the priests alike. Every bot with an interrupt
also fires it on every cast, so the interrupts are spent together and a Dark
Mending lands in the gap. At Baron Geddon, the Living Bomb carrier runs from
the group and no healer goes with it, so the carrier dies.

WHAT IT DOES

1. Damage target selection excludes Sulfuron while a Flamewaker Priest is alive
   and within spell distance and line of sight of the bot, in the same hook
   that already excludes Majordomo. A priest that is excluded, out of range or
   out of sight does not count, so the bot is never left without a target. It
   applies to the DPS target type only.
2. While Sulfuron is present, a multiplier blocks the interrupt actions (kick,
   pummel, shield bash, counterspell, earth shock) for every bot except the
   two assigned. The assigned are the two living members with an interrupt and
   the lowest guids in the group, so the bots agree without talking.
3. Exactly one healer, the living one without a bomb and with the lowest guid,
   follows a Living Bomb carrier until it is within 25 yards, outside the blast
   and inside healing range. The movement is allowed while Inferno is active.
   No other bot is given a reason to leave the group.

WHAT THIS PATCH DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO

It does not change the Inferno move-away or the return to the boss (the
existing Inferno trigger and multiplier handle both). It does not touch
Golemagg, Core Hounds or the Majordomo series (patches 0017 to 0021). It keys
on creature and spell ids, so no other encounter is affected. Priest
exclusion is an exclusion, not a priority: the fork exposes no priority hook.

WHEN THIS PATCH SHOULD BE DELETED

When the fork's Molten Core strategy orders the Sulfuron priests, assigns the
Dark Mending interrupts and sends a healer after the bomb carrier itself.

